WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.090
I want my company to have an intelligence
of its own.

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:08.340
Right now, it runs on good people, each
holding a piece of the picture.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:10.400
One remembers the promises.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.240
One knows the real costs.

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:14.660
One hears what customers keep asking for.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.060
And someone has to hold it all together
and think of the next question.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.140
Here, that's me.

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:26.970
I've read nearly every day for thirty-five
years, mostly science fiction.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:31.733
I still want the ship's computer: the one
that knows where we're heading, how much

00:00:31.773 --> 00:00:35.200
fuel is left, and why the captain's
brilliant plan won't work.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:36.770
Even when I'm the captain.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:41.670
At Head Aero, our aviation business, we
built the first version.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.550
We call it HAI.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:48.730
A colleague dropped a link in our group
chat: "What could we make here?"

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:56.090
Behind it: a Boeing 757, and 32,424 pages
of records.

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:59.430
HAI caught a row the seller's spreadsheet
skipped.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.670
The best part wasn't in the folder.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:07.532
In our own email, it found the same two
engines, offered to us in 2023, and my

00:01:07.572 --> 00:01:10.000
reply: "Where are they located?"

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.780
At least one of us remembered.

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:17.591
It found a customer we'd quoted for the
same part number, and proposed a deal: a

00:01:17.631 --> 00:01:20.140
partner buys, we sell selected parts.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.710
Our own history turned a folder into an
opportunity.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:26.970
But this is only the beginning.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.060
Imagine it doesn't wait for anyone to ask.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.535
Say customers keep asking for next-day
delivery, and the team keeps pulling it

00:01:35.575 --> 00:01:36.610
off as a favour.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:42.034
HAI notices the pattern, and brings us a
question: are we giving away something

00:01:42.074 --> 00:01:43.450
people would pay for?

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:48.872
Like a seasoned analyst, it looks at who
asks, how often, what it costs, and what

00:01:48.912 --> 00:01:50.250
the team can handle.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:55.887
Our dispatcher adds what no system
recorded: half those rushes were our own

00:01:55.927 --> 00:01:56.870
late picking.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:02.618
So it changes course: fix our delay first,
then price speed for the customers who

00:02:02.658 --> 00:02:03.700
truly need it.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.480
One number is missing: what a rush really
costs.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.638
So it builds a small tool to measure it,
tests it on last month's invoices, and

00:02:12.678 --> 00:02:14.050
hands it to the team.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:20.160
We set the limits: three customers, one
month, a fixed price.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.090
HAI runs the trial, from the offers to the
follow-ups.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:27.130
A month later, it reports back.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.180
Two customers were worth it.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:30.570
One wasn't.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.910
Its next proposal starts from what
actually happened.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:39.540
Our dispatcher shapes a new service
without becoming an AI engineer.

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:42.930
I weigh an opportunity instead of
inventing it.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.100
Models will get better.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:46.560
Tools will change.

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:47.680
People move on.

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:51.160
What the company has learned stays, and
keeps growing.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.620
We still choose where the company goes.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:57.880
But we shouldn't have to think of every
possibility alone.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:03.820
That's why we're building HAI Seed: so
your company can have an intelligence of

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:07.130
its own, without building an AI department
first.

